# OptiKPI V2.0 Smoke Test Automation — Project Conventions

## Tech Stack

| Technology | Purpose |
|------------|---------|
| TypeScript | All page objects, step definitions, hooks, and utilities |
| Playwright | Browser automation (Chromium) |
| Cucumber.js v12 | BDD feature execution with Gherkin syntax |
| Extent Reports | HTML test reporting with screenshots |
| ts-node | TypeScript execution without precompilation |
| Node.js >= 20.17 | Runtime |

---

## Architecture Rules

### Page Object Model (POM)

Every browser interaction MUST go through a Page Object class.

```
BasePage (src/pages/base.page.ts)
  ├── LoginPage
  ├── DashboardPage
  ├── AudiencePage
  ├── CampaignPage
  ├── WorkflowPage
  └── components/
      ├── NavigationBarComponent
      └── DateTimePickerComponent
```

- All page classes extend `BasePage`
- Selectors are `private readonly` inside a `sel` object — never exposed publicly
- Use `BasePage` helpers (`click`, `fill`, `getText`, `isVisible`, `waitForVisible`) — do not call `page.locator(...)` directly inside page methods unless necessary
- Step definitions instantiate page objects via helper functions: `const getPage = (world) => new PageClass(world.page)`

### Step Definitions

- One step file per module: `audience.steps.ts`, `campaign.steps.ts`, `workflow.steps.ts`, etc.
- Steps MUST NOT contain raw selectors — delegate all locator logic to page objects
- Use `ExtentTestManager.logPass(...)` at the end of every passing step
- Use `ExtentTestManager.logFail(...)` or `throw new Error(...)` for failures
- Store shared state on `this` (the World): `this['currentAudienceTitle']`, `this['currentCampaignName']`, etc.

### Feature Files

- One feature file per module in `features/`
- Smoke tests use `@SmokeTest` + `@ST-<MODULE>-<NN>` tags
- Regression tests use `@Regression` + `@TC-<MODULE>-<NN>` tags
- Prerequisite scenarios use `@TestPreparation`
- Step wording must match existing step definitions exactly (case-sensitive)

### Test Data (names.json)

- Use `saveNameEntry(type, title)` or `saveNameEntries([...])` to persist test data
- Use `readNameJson()` or `getNameEntry(type)` to retrieve
- Always use `withFileLock` (built into save/read helpers) for concurrent access
- The runner resets `names.json` to `{}` at startup — do not rely on data persisting across runs
- Valid keys: `'audience'`, `'campaign'`, `'workflow'`, `'existingAudience'`, or scenario tag strings like `'TC-AUD-REG-05'`

